Explanation of bug:
 
acceptOffer is missing an ownership check. rejectOffer starts with "if(tiles[x][y].owner != msg.sender) return;" but acceptOffer has no such line:
  
>  function acceptOffer(uint8 x, uint8 y, uint8 i) // accepts the offer at index (1-10)
>  {
>        tiles[x][y].owner.send(tiles[x][y].offers[i]); // send offer money to oldowner
>        tiles[x][y].owner = tiles[x][y].offerers[i]; // new owner is the offerer
>        delete tiles[x][y].offerers; // delete all offerers
>        delete tiles[x][y].offers; // delete all offers
>        return;
>  }
   
So anyone, not just the tile's owner, can accept any offer on any tile. To steal a tile, place the minimum offer (0.01 ETH) with makeOffer and immediately accept it yourself with acceptOffer. 
The 0.01 ETH goes to the old owner and the tile is yours. Anyone can also force a sale of a tile they don't own by accepting someone else's offer on it.
The bytecode on the chain confirms this: acceptOffer never reads msg.sender, while rejectOffer does
  
